{"source": "designer", "id": 52, "type": "plan", "message": "Wrote designs/wall_bracket.py: an L-shaped shelf bracket printed shelf-face-down (shelf face z=0, wall face x=0, width along Y). The L is one XZ profile with the inner_radius fillet blended in 2D and a 44-degree self-supporting chamfer at the bed corner (horizontal leg = outer_radius, per the library edge_break convention), extruded across the width. Free plate corners get corner_radius in plan; the room-side convex edge chain is filleted with min(outer_radius, corner_radius/2) while the wall face and bed edges stay sharp for flat contact. A centreline pentagon gusset (ramp edges filleted with gusset_edge_radius before union, base sunk half a plate into both legs) spans gusset_reach of each free leg. Wall holes: 2x M4 counterbored_hole with teardrop, axis X, opening on the room face x=thickness, centred on the free wall leg. Shelf holes: 2x M4 counterbored_hole, axis Z, opening on the bed face z=0 (screw goes up into the shelf), centred on the free shelf leg. All hardware sizes come from standard_parts(); every cutter/boss is wrapped in feature(). PARAMS match the brief exactly. run_check(\"wall_bracket\") full run passed Execute, Geometry, Printability, Renders and Sweep (105.9 s); metrics: bbox 80x60x80, 4 holes recognised with correct axes/spacing, unsupported area 68.7 mm2 (the two bridged shelf counterbore floors only), support_risk 1.38 %, min wall 4 mm. A 29-case in-session corner sweep also built valid single solids at every PARAMS extreme."}
